    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe request now accepts a structured address (`addressLine1`, optional `addressLine2`, plus the existing `city`/`postcode`) while the flat `address` stays accepted for backward compatibility.\n\n**Three files touched:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` string properties to `OwnerFields` (so both the request `OwnerFieldsDto` and response `OwnerDto` carry them), and removed `address` from the `required` list so a structured owner (no flat `address`) still passes bean validation. `city` stays required.\n\n2. **`OwnerFieldsValidator`** \u2014 replaced the single normalization line in `validate` with a call to a new small `composeAddress` helper. It normalizes `addressLine1` (and `addressLine2`), and when `addressLine1` is non-blank composes `address` = normalized line1 (with a single space + normalized line2 when line2 is present); otherwise it falls back to the normalized flat `address`. Because the composed value is written back into `address` *before* the existing required-fields check, validity (\"address in either form, plus city\") is enforced by the unchanged `rejectIfEmptyOrWhitespace` loop, and every downstream reader of `owner.getAddress()` automatically sees the structured-when-present value.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping(target = \"addressLine1\", source = \"address\")` so the response echoes the normalized line, equal to the composed `address`.\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\n- No change to the large `Owner` entity or any DB schema (Hibernate `ddl-auto=none` on the test profile would otherwise force schema edits across all four DB dialects).\n- The only pre-existing method edited is `validate`, and only one line of it; the new behaviour lives in a fresh, low-complexity helper. The mapper change is a single annotation on an interface method.\n\nHousehold hash, postcode validation and locality already read `postcode`/`city` (shared across both request forms) and the now-composed `address`, so they pick up the structured fields with no edits.\n\n`mvn test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
